# Claude Code session files and local tooling
.claude-local/
# ⚠ `.claude/*` and NOT `.claude/`. With a trailing slash git never descends into the directory, so
# a later negation cannot re-include anything inside it. The glob form is what makes the exception
# below actually work.
.claude/*
# The review-gate definitions are TRACKED. They used to live only in `~/.claude/commands/` with a
# hand-copied backup in `.claude-local/commands/` — unversioned, invisible to any reader, and 4 of
# the 8 had silently drifted apart. Claude Code reads project commands from here, so tracking them
# means exactly one copy, which is also the copy a reviewer can read.
!.claude/commands/
# ⚠ THE WHOLE GUARD RECORD IS TRACKED, AND IT HAD TO BE ALL THREE PARTS OR NONE. `settings.json`
# carries the permissions AND the `hooks` wiring; the scripts that wiring points at are in
# `tools/verify/claude_hooks/`. A clone therefore inherits the guards rather than an appearance of
# them. `settings.local.json` stays ignored and is now empty — it holds nothing load-bearing.
#
# Why all three: tracking the wiring alone would point at scripts a clone does not have, and a hook
# whose command is missing fails OPEN — a repo that looks armed and is not, which is strictly worse
# than one that is visibly bare. Tracking the scripts alone records what the guards ARE and not
# which are ARMED. Measured 2026-08-23 (`GUARD-1`): the tracked file had held `permissions.allow`
# only — seven wildcards, no `deny`, no `hooks` — while all 36 deny rules and both hook events sat
# in the ignored file, so the record of which guards are wired existed in no repository at all,
# which is exactly what tracking it had been claimed to fix.
!.claude/settings.json

# Local MCP tooling (standalone repo, not part of the math publication)
imap-email-mcp/

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Lean 4 / Lake ---
# Ignore the build artifacts and local toolchain
.lake/
build/
lean_packages/
